{"html":"<h1 id=\"vkf-style-guide\">VKF Style Guide</h1>\n<p>This guide covers canonical VKF forms and repository documentation style. General software-design advice does not belong here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"documentation\">Documentation</h2>\n<p>Wrap Markdown prose at 80 columns. Leave code fences, tables, badges, HTML, link targets, and generated markers intact when wrapping would damage their syntax or generated form.</p>\n<h2 id=\"functions-and-returns\">Functions And Returns</h2>\n<p>Keep a single-expression function on one row and use its implicit result:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-1\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-1\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Functions And Returns\" spellcheck=\"false\">square(value:num) -&gt; num: value^2</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p>Keep a function or nominal constructor whose complete body is a bare null or local-scope return on one row too:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-2\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-2\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Functions And Returns\" spellcheck=\"false\">empty(): @\nPoint(x:num, y:num): :</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p>Use explicit <code>@:</code> to make the result of a multi-row function visible:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-3\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-3\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Functions And Returns\" spellcheck=\"false\">shift(value:num) -&gt; num:\n    squared: value^2\n    @: squared + 1</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<h2 id=\"pipe-layout\">Pipe Layout</h2>\n<p>Keep a single-expression pipeline inline:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-4\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-4\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Pipe Layout\" spellcheck=\"false\">ret: (..3 &gt;&gt; $^2)</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p>Semicolons are suitable for a short multi-row stage. Each semicolon begins a new row at the stage's current logical indentation; following spaces are ignored:</p>\n<pre class=\"vkf-static\" data-vkf-source><code>ret: (array &gt;&gt; doubled: $ * 2; doubled + 1)</code></pre>\n<p>A parenthesized multiline pipeline is valid, but direct block evaluation is the canonical form. Align each following <code>&gt;&gt;</code> with the first stage:</p>\n<pre class=\"vkf-static\" data-vkf-source><code>ret:\n    array &gt;&gt;\n        doubled: $ * 2\n        doubled + 1\n    &gt;&gt;\n        $^2</code></pre>\n<p>The final pipeline value becomes <code>ret</code> automatically.</p>\n<h2 id=\"scope-names\">Scope Names</h2>\n<p>After spilling a record into local scope, consistently use its exposed names:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-5\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-5\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Scope Names\" spellcheck=\"false\">measure(system:System) -&gt; num:\n    :system\n    @: |positions.0| * masses.0</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p>Do not mix <code>positions</code> with redundant forms such as <code>system.positions</code> in the same spilled scope.</p>\n<p>Spill a standard-library module when using its members throughout an example. Keep the resulting expressions focused on the operation:</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-6\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.7</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-6\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Scope Names\" spellcheck=\"false\">:.math\nx: [..512] / 256 - 1\ny: sin(x * pi)</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<h2 id=\"iteration\">Iteration</h2>\n<p>Use a range pipe for fixed unit-step iteration:</p>\n<pre class=\"vkf-static\" data-vkf-source><code>total: 0\n..9 &gt;&gt; .total+: $</code></pre>\n<p>Use <code>condition?&gt;</code> when termination depends on changing program state rather than a fixed range.</p>\n<h2 id=\"vectors-and-indices\">Vectors And Indices</h2>\n<p>Use vector operations instead of manually separating components. A literal member or index uses <code>.name</code> or <code>.0</code>; a computed index uses <code>.(expression)</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"vkf-static\" data-vkf-source><code>.position+: velocity * timestep\nvalue: positions.(index)\nfirst: positions.0</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"updates\">Updates</h2>\n<p>Declare with <code>name:</code>. Update the declared name with <code>.name:</code> or a compound form such as <code>.name+:</code>. Updating a selected record field or container element keeps the selection on the left:</p>\n<pre class=\"vkf-static\" data-vkf-source><code>count: 0\n.count+: 1\npoint.x: 4\nvalues.(index): 7</code></pre>","headings":[{"level":1,"title":"VKF Style Guide","id":"vkf-style-guide"},{"level":2,"title":"Documentation","id":"documentation"},{"level":2,"title":"Functions And Returns","id":"functions-and-returns"},{"level":2,"title":"Pipe Layout","id":"pipe-layout"},{"level":2,"title":"Scope Names","id":"scope-names"},{"level":2,"title":"Iteration","id":"iteration"},{"level":2,"title":"Vectors And Indices","id":"vectors-and-indices"},{"level":2,"title":"Updates","id":"updates"}],"examples":[{"id":"example-1","source":"square(value:num) -> num: value^2","title":"Functions And Returns"},{"id":"example-2","source":"empty(): @\nPoint(x:num, y:num): :","title":"Functions And Returns"},{"id":"example-3","source":"shift(value:num) -> num:\n    squared: value^2\n    @: squared + 1","title":"Functions And Returns"},{"id":"example-4","source":"ret: (..3 >> $^2)","title":"Pipe Layout"},{"id":"example-5","source":"measure(system:System) -> num:\n    :system\n    @: |positions.0| * masses.0","title":"Scope Names"},{"id":"example-6","source":":.math\nx: [..512] / 256 - 1\ny: sin(x * pi)","title":"Scope Names"}],"source":"docs/style-guide.md","route":"style.html","releaseCatalog":{"schema":"vektor-flow/release-catalog-v1","latest":"0.4.7","latestBrowserRuntime":{"version":"0.4.7","url":"https://vektorflow.org/runtimes/v0.4.7/vkf-shared-compiler.wasm?sha256=d906c29e80bb4fa6ed3999379ad8679bc55a6ba708a50483fe09147437a1b3e9"},"releases":[{"version":"0.4.7","tag":"v0.4.7","status":"published","browserRuntimeWasm":"https://vektorflow.org/runtimes/v0.4.7/vkf-shared-compiler.wasm?sha256=d906c29e80bb4fa6ed3999379ad8679bc55a6ba708a50483fe09147437a1b3e9","benchmarkTier":"patch","benchmark":{"summary":"Local Windows, Linux, and Firefox comparisons; unmeasured cells remain explicit.","browser":null,"evidenceUrl":"https://vektorflow.org/performance.html"},"downloads":{"windows":{"installer":"https://vektorflow.org/downloads/v0.4.7/vektor-flow-windows-x64-setup.exe?sha256=2f656c5cb9f3d4f8e544a2157c54dce1d73004e7296e842573da1acada27a955","archive":"https://vektorflow.org/downloads/v0.4.7/vektor-flow-windows-x64.zip?sha256=ca05457ebf22f79